course: dictionary
lesson: 14217
title: Sounds and secrets
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words sound like what they describe. Murmuring is one of them: say it slowly and you can almost hear a soft, low sound. «The stream was murmuring over the stones.» You can picture water running quietly, so murmuring must mean making a low, soft sound.
explain: Murmuring can also mean speaking very quietly, so people nearby can hardly hear. «The two girls were murmuring behind the library door.» The words around it, behind the door, show that the girls were talking in a soft, secret way.
explain: Murmuring can be a verb, an adjective or a noun. As a noun, murmurings are quiet complaints or rumours. «There were murmurings about the new bus times.» Nobody was shouting. The context tells you people were grumbling quietly and were not happy.
fact: Murmuring means making a low, soft, continuous sound, like a stream, bees or the wind in leaves.
fact: Murmuring also means saying something quietly, so it is hard to hear.
fact: As a noun, «murmurings» means quiet complaints or rumours.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, the river is always murmuring and chattering.
fact: In the Bible, the Israelites murmured in the desert, which means they grumbled against Moses.
exercise: «The bees were murmuring in the garden all afternoon.» What was making the murmuring sound? | The shouting children | *The bees | The rain on the window | The gardener
exercise: «She stood at the window, murmuring to her baby until it fell asleep.» What does murmuring mean here? | *Saying something softly, so it is hard to hear | Shouting loudly at the baby | Singing a loud, happy song | Crying with a loud voice
exercise: «There were murmurings in the class about the test.» What are the murmurings? | *Quiet complaints or rumours | Happy cheers | Sleepy yawns | Loud songs
test: «Sam could hear the murmuring leaves above the tent.» What is making the murmuring sound? | The tent | *The leaves | The sun | Sam
test: Mia says murmuring means shouting. Is she right? | *No, murmuring is soft and quiet | Yes, murmuring means loud shouting | Yes, it is a loud sound like thunder | No, it means very happy
exam: What does «murmurings» mean in «There were murmurings about the new bus times»? | *Quiet complaints or rumours | Loud cheers | Sounds from the bus engine | Soft, happy songs
